    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system across the two places the membership logic lives.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `getMembershipPoints()` and rewrote `getMembershipLevel()`:\n- `getMembershipPoints()`: starts at 0, `+2` for an email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+ (new `hasLargeHousehold()` helper over `householdSize`), `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- `getMembershipLevel()`: now derived from points \u2014 `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` read-only integer property to the Owner schema and updated `membershipLevel` (description + `maximum: 4`). Since the DTO is generated from this spec at build time and mapped via MapStruct by property name, both fields now flow into the API response automatically.\n\nBoth the old rule (level from factors) is gone and the new fields are returned. The acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
