    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The path is `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1` + `POST /owners` from the generated `OwnersApi`. All the real logic lives in the **controller** \u2014 the service layer is just a thin `save`.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; with security disabled it's `permitAll` and not evaluated).\n2. **Bean Validation on the `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, interface is `@Validated`) \u2014 failures short-circuit to **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`. Field constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)` (no pattern here)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` ISO dates (optional)\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraints (optional Boolean)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Inside the controller body (in execution order)\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`); `id` and `pets` are ignored. *Side-effect:* `Owner.setEmail` **lower-cases the email**.\n4. **`normalizeAndValidate(owner)`**, in this internal order \u2014 any failure returns a raw **400** (these bypass the ControllerAdvice):\n   - a. **Address normalization** \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`; blank \u2192 400. *(mutates address)*\n   - b. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 assumes `+61`, strips non-digits, must be 8\u201315 digits and pass national-length check; unconvertible \u2192 400. *(mutates telephone)*\n   - c. **Disposable-email block** \u2014 rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 400.\n   - d. **Postcode region-range** check (`isPostcodeValid`) \u2192 400.\n   - e. **Future `registrationDate`** \u2192 400.\n   - f. **Default & roll registration date** \u2014 null defaults to today, then rolled forward to a business day. *(mutates registrationDate)*\n5. **Daily limit** (`isDailyLimitReached`) \u2014 \u2265100 owners already on that registration date \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS** (reads all owners via `findAllOwners()`).\n6. Compute **`sharesHousehold`** flag from the DTO.\n7. **`assignHousehold`** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName | postcode)`. *(side-effect)*\n8. **`checkForConflicts`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`:\n   - a. **Household duplicate** (`isHouseholdDuplicate`) \u2192 **409**.\n   - b. **City at capacity** (\u226550 owners in city) \u2192 **409**.\n9. **`assignDerivedAttributes`** sets, in order *(all side-effects)*:\n   - a. `customerCode` = `<region>-<sha8(telephone+lastName)>`\n   - b. `namesakeCount`\n   - c. `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners that day)\n   - d. `householdSize`\n   - e. `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (from a soft-duplicate lookup)\n10. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`@Transactional`). No pets cascade on create (pets were ignored in mapping).\n11. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=...\")`.\n12. **Build 201 response** \u2014 `created(owner)`: `Location: /api/owners/{id}` + `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## What is NOT on this path (checked)\n\nNo `@InitBinder`, no custom Owner validator (`PetAgeValidator` is pets-only), no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` or JPA auditing, no application events, no emails/notifications, and no password encoding or role assignment. Entity-level constraints (`@NotEmpty`, E.164 `@Pattern`, `@Email` on `Owner`/`Person`) exist and could fire at Hibernate flush, but the controller's own checks run first.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the controller's internal failures (steps 4, 5, 8) return **bare status codes with no body**, unlike the DTO validation in step 2 which returns a structured `ProblemDetail`."
  },
